"In 2025, Canada produced a total of 6,256,639 barrels per day of oil and petroleum liquids, of which 4,963,935 barrels per day was classified as crude oil.  This means crude oil accounted for approximately 79% of Canada's total daily oil production that year.  The remaining 1,181,366 barrels per day consisted of natural gas plant liquids (NGPL). 

In 2024, crude oil production averaged 5.13 million barrels per day as part of the total crude oil and equivalents output, with the majority of this production coming from Alberta's oil sands. "
